  Which brings us to the usual discussion of "Can a lujvo mean something
other than the sum of it's parts?"  e.g can you have "nikyge'u" mean"g1=n1
is an exaggerated creature/character (such as a dog made of nickel) of
origin g2" ? (http://jbovlaste.lojban.org/dict/nikyge'u)  There are
differing opinions on the matter.  The CLL says, "

The meaning of a lujvo is controlled by --- but is not the same as --- the
meaning of the tanru from which the lujvo was constructed" (12.2), which
would seem to suggest not, but many say it's perfectly acceptable.
                           --gejyspa

